%% DGT Studio Pro — 02 library and analysis
%% Re-authored 9 Aug 2026 against the tree at 5f82de7 plus the comment-reduction
%% working tree, read from source
%% (LibraryDestination.narrowedPairs / filteredGames / gamesInDisplayOrder,
%%  PGNStore.importPGN / delete / backfillLibraryIndices / classify,
%%  AnalysisQueueController, GameAnalysisDriver).

flowchart TD

    ENTER(("Library destination")) --> WARM["On appear: healPlayersIfNeeded - the two player<br/>backfills behind a CONVERGED STAMP D75′, so the<br/>healed steady state skips the scan entirely -<br/>then backfillClassifications, which carries a<br/>Predicate: the converged case fetches ZERO rows"]

    WARM --> QUERY["Query PGN sorted by importedAt, reverse<br/>- the array's ARRIVAL order. A sort always runs<br/>downstream, so this shows through only as the<br/>tie order among equal ordinals, which are legal:<br/>D58′ does not make the index unique"]

    subgraph IMPORT["Import - the one door that admits a star result"]
        IMP0["Choose files, or paste PGN text"] --> IMP1["PGNParser - annotations stripped to ! and ?<br/>check and mate suffixes survive verbatim"]
        IMP1 --> IMP2{"Required tags present<br/>and well formed?"}
        IMP2 -->|"no"| IMP3["Refused: missingRequiredTags<br/>or malformedPGN"]
        IMP2 -->|"yes"| IMP4["Compute the content hash - MD5 over the<br/>normalised recipe. ONE recipe, two spellings"]
        IMP4 --> IMP5{"A row already<br/>carries that hash?"}
        IMP5 -->|"yes"| IMP6["THROWS duplicate, carrying the existing id<br/>and name. It does NOT return the existing row -<br/>do not infer the contract from the name"]
        IMP5 -->|"no"| IMP7["Insert, then resolvePlayers D9′ - the ONE<br/>creation door, identity folded to lowercase with<br/>whitespace collapsed, diacritics PRESERVED.<br/>Then classify D34′ - engine-free, ECO and the<br/>checkmate type together: ten motifs since D65′,<br/>precedence NARROWEST FIRST, and the name split<br/>into family and variation at the first colon D35′.<br/>The ordinal is read off the FILENAME D58′"]
    end

    IMP7 --> QUERY
    IMP3 --> ENTER
    IMP6 --> ENTER

    IMP0 -.-> STAR2
    STAR2["This is the REACHABLE source of a star result.<br/>importPGN admits it deliberately; Decision 3 is<br/>enforced at the ARCHIVE door only - diagram 01"]

    IMP7 -.-> NOVAL
    NOVAL["LEGALITY IS NOT CHECKED HERE. Import parses<br/>SHAPE - tags, tokens, comments, variations<br/>stripped - and never replays. The app's only<br/>replay validators are Get Info's Move Text tab<br/>and Game.init on a Board load, so an imported<br/>file can carry an unreplayable ply for months,<br/>and the first surface to replay it reports it.<br/>Strict SAN applies there: a capture written<br/>without its x reads as no legal move matches -<br/>a dialect refusal, not corruption"]

    subgraph NARROW["Narrowing - sidebar, then search, then chips. Narrowing ONLY, so the stages compose"]
        QUERY --> N1["Sidebar smart-tag filter D12′<br/>matching is an in-memory fold over TagRule,<br/>never a Predicate: a stored Codable rule<br/>array cannot be queried in the store"]
        N1 --> N2["Search text - SearchMatch.Query folded ONCE<br/>per pass, matched per game. Every field,<br/>always: a query already names its own field"]
        N2 --> N3["Token chips - result and analysis facets.<br/>OR within a facet, AND across facets.<br/>Analysed? has ONE spelling since D67′:<br/>PGN.hasScoredPly - an all-nil array is not<br/>analysis - read by the chips, the badges and<br/>every gate alike, saved tags included D68′"]
    end

    N1 -.-> MEMO
    MEMO["The GameRecord projection is MEMOIZED D70′ on an<br/>explicit content key - the fields the folds read,<br/>plus the queue's counters as the analysis signal,<br/>NEVER the evaluations array. Since D78′ the<br/>narrowing walk and the sort ride the same<br/>discipline: filter, query, chips and comparators<br/>join the key, so the walk and the O n log n run<br/>once per CHANGE, not per render"]

    N3 --> N4["Column sort - LAST stage, after every narrowing.<br/>ONE value per destination since D69′, set by the<br/>header OR the View Options panel, PERSISTED - a<br/>sort is a standing preference now, no longer<br/>session-only. Defaults to the ordinal descending<br/>D58′: the Library opens on the highest-numbered<br/>file, un-numbered games at the bottom"]

    N4 -.-> SORTNOTE
    SORTNOTE["Why the sort lives in the DESTINATION and not<br/>in the table: three things downstream read<br/>DISPLAY ORDER rather than the screen. D24′<br/>numbers exported filenames from it, the analysis<br/>queue crunches top-to-bottom as shown, and D56′<br/>makes it tab order - all through<br/>gamesInDisplayOrder. Sorting inside the table<br/>would reorder pixels while all three kept<br/>numbering from the unsorted array. Nothing would<br/>fail; the filenames would simply stop matching<br/>the screen"]

    N4 --> FG["filteredGames<br/>ONE walk per render over the memoized<br/>projection, threaded to the empty gate, the<br/>subtitle census, the mode view, the badge set<br/>and the inspector"]

    FG --> EMPTY{"Anything left?"}
    EMPTY -->|"no, and narrowed"| E1["No matches - clear the search or the chips"]
    EMPTY -->|"no, and not narrowed"| E2["No games - import some"]
    EMPTY -->|"yes"| MODE{"View mode?<br/>ONE shared AppStorage key across<br/>both collection destinations"}

    E1 --> ENTER
    E2 --> IMP0

    MODE -->|"list"| MD1["Table - an Analysis column with the<br/>glyph as a live control"]
    MODE -->|"columns"| MD2["Finder-flat: list plus detail pane,<br/>a trailing verdict glyph per row"]
    MODE -->|"icons"| MD3["Grid - rubber band plus arrow keys,<br/>a corner badge on the card sheet"]
    MODE -->|"gallery"| MD4["Filmstrip - left/right steps it,<br/>the same corner badge"]

    MD1 --> PAINTED
    MD2 --> PAINTED
    MD3 --> PAINTED
    MD4 --> PAINTED

    PAINTED["Rows painted"]
    PAINTED -.-> BADGE
    BADGE["D72′: analysis state is legible in EVERY mode -<br/>green check analysed, red x not, a bare turning<br/>gear while the engine has it. All four surfaces<br/>read ONE ambient runningID plus the memoized<br/>analyzedIDs set, so no row decodes a blob and<br/>no two modes can disagree"]

    PAINTED -->|"click, or rubber band"| SEL
    PAINTED -->|"Cmd-A"| CMDA

    SEL["Selection"]

    CMDA["The SYSTEM's Edit, Select All via onCommand on<br/>the responder chain - not a keyboardShortcut of<br/>our own. Takes the NARROWED list, which is<br/>filteredGames' standing contract rather than a<br/>new one"] --> SEL

    CMDA -.-> CMDANOTE
    CMDANOTE["Three behaviours fall out of the MECHANISM,<br/>and they are why onCommand beat a shortcut:<br/>1. Cmd-A inside the search field selects TEXT -<br/>the field is first responder and answers first.<br/>2. List and columns are Tables, so NSTableView<br/>answers and this handler never runs - the set<br/>is identical because the table was built from<br/>the same narrowed array.<br/>3. A nil action on an empty list leaves the menu<br/>item DISABLED by the system.<br/>Icons and gallery have no such responder, and<br/>for them this is the whole implementation"]

    SEL -.-> CMDACOST
    CMDACOST["Cmd-A selects what the render PAINTED,<br/>deliberately not what filteredGames would answer<br/>at action time - the opposite of the rule below,<br/>for the opposite reason. Select All must mean the<br/>rows on screen or it means something the user<br/>cannot check.<br/>KNOWN COST: the icons grid's anchorID is out of<br/>reach, so an arrow after Cmd-A steps from the<br/>last card CLICKED, not from the selection"]

    SEL --> ACT{"Action? The toolbar keeps only Import,<br/>the conditional Reconcile, and the queue's<br/>status item - Analyse, Export and Delete<br/>moved to the ROW MENUS on 6 Aug,<br/>with their keys riding along"}

    ACT -->|"Open - D56′"| OP0{"More than ten games?"}
    OP0 -->|"yes"| OP1["Confirm first - the ONE bulk action that<br/>confirms on count rather than on destruction"]
    OP0 -->|"no"| OP2["One window per game, in DISPLAY order,<br/>because that order is visible as TAB order"]
    OP1 --> OP2
    OP2 --> DONE

    ACT -->|"Export - Cmd-E, D24′"| EX0["gamesInDisplayOrder - re-derived FRESH,<br/>because an action fires long after the fold<br/>that painted the screen"]
    EX0 --> EX1["PGNSerializer - byte-pinned to the DGT<br/>reference files. LF endings, nine tags in fixed<br/>order, tag-form names, one full move per line.<br/>A numbered game exports under ITS ordinal, the<br/>rest under batch position D58′.<br/>Classification is NOT written: derived truth<br/>is not interchange"]
    EX1 --> EX2["Batch writes one numbered file per game and<br/>OVERWRITES same-named files silently D32′ -<br/>the export is a pure function of the rows"]
    EX2 --> DONE

    ACT -->|"Analyse - Cmd-R"| AN0["Enqueue in display order - a pure FIFO queue<br/>with dedupe, behind the ONE app-global<br/>controller: one driver, one engine subprocess,<br/>never two racing. A single game is a batch<br/>of one"]
    AN0 --> AN0B["The pass is a PLAN, not the whole game D74′:<br/>the classified book prefix is skipped - the<br/>table already names those positions - and a ply<br/>scored at or above the target depth is KEPT, so<br/>re-analysis DEEPENS instead of restarting.<br/>A fully satisfied game never spawns the engine"]
    AN0B --> AN1["Bundled Stockfish over UCI at the configured<br/>depth, hash and threads - Settings bind to<br/>reality since M11, Syzygy path sent LAST when a<br/>folder is configured. Teardown must complete<br/>even when cancelled, and must strand no waiter"]
    AN1 --> AN2["ONE evaluation per ply folded in memory, each<br/>with the depth it was searched at D74′,<br/>ONE SAVE PER EXIT D71′ - done, cancelled or<br/>failed alike. The per-ply save it replaced<br/>invalidated every Query in the app once per ply"]
    AN2 --> AN3["The queue WINDOW - openWindow by id, no wrapper<br/>type to mint - shows the live search, both<br/>clocks, the line and the finished log.<br/>The toolbar keeps only a status item: a turning<br/>gear while live, a warning after a failed drain<br/>until Clear acknowledges it<br/>DRILL-DOWN: diagram 04"]
    AN3 --> DONE

    AN0 -.-> SLEEP
    SLEEP["A live batch is a SECOND sleep-inhibition cause<br/>with its own Settings gate D66′ - an overnight<br/>drain survives idle sleep; the display still dims.<br/>The engine is RELEASED at drain: the next batch<br/>pays one fresh handshake, nothing idles in<br/>Activity Monitor"]

    ACT -->|"Edit Moves"| MV0["NOT HERE since D59′. The Library inspector's<br/>PGN section shows the movetext and no longer<br/>offers to edit it - the pencil D54′ put there<br/>lasted one day. The door is Get Info's<br/>MOVE TEXT tab<br/>DRILL-DOWN: diagram 04"]

    ACT -->|"Delete - Cmd-Backspace"| DL0["Confirm - reached from the row menu, whose<br/>Cmd-Backspace is the app's ONLY delete key:<br/>plain Backspace does nothing, and the toolbar<br/>button that carried the shortcut is gone"]
    DL0 --> DL1["Stop any running pass on these games FIRST -<br/>synchronously, before the store delete, so the<br/>engine never writes into a tombstone. Then<br/>compute the stranded players BEFORE the first<br/>delete D50′ - asking afterwards bets on SwiftData<br/>having already propagated the nullify"]
    DL1 --> DL2["One transaction: delete the games, then the<br/>players their deletion stranded.<br/>Deleting the GAME takes its seat tags with it,<br/>so nothing is left to re-resolve"]
    DL2 --> DONE

    ACT -->|"Reconcile - toolbar, present only while<br/>some game lacks an ordinal"| RC0["D58′'s folder backfill: point at the folder the<br/>PGNs live in. Files match rows by CONTENT HASH,<br/>never by filename - the folder writes full names,<br/>the serializer given names - and each match is<br/>stamped with its filename's ordinal.<br/>An existing ordinal is never overwritten; one<br/>save outside the loop; ALWAYS reports, because a<br/>silent scan looks like a scan that never ran"]
    RC0 --> DONE

    ACT -->|"Get Info - Cmd-I"| GI0["Get Info WINDOW, not a sheet<br/>DRILL-DOWN: diagram 04"]

    ACT -->|"Open in a tab - Cmd-O"| REV["Review on the Board<br/>DRILL-DOWN: diagram 01"]

    DONE(("Back to the collection"))

    %% ---- shared class vocabulary: identical block in all five files ----
    classDef act   fill:#e8eef7,stroke:#5b7fb0,color:#12243d
    classDef dec   fill:#fdf0d5,stroke:#c9a227,color:#3d2f04
    classDef bad   fill:#fbe4e4,stroke:#c0504d,color:#4a1210
    classDef note  fill:#efe6f7,stroke:#8064a2,color:#2c1b3d
    classDef drill fill:#e3f2e3,stroke:#4f8a4f,color:#123312
    classDef term  fill:#2f3640,stroke:#1b1f24,color:#ffffff

    class WARM,QUERY,IMP0,IMP1,IMP4,IMP7,N1,N2,N3,N4,FG,MD1,MD2,MD3,MD4,PAINTED,SEL,CMDA,E1,E2,OP1,OP2,EX0,EX1,EX2,AN0,AN0B,AN1,AN2,AN3,DL0,DL1,DL2,RC0 act
    class IMP2,IMP5,EMPTY,MODE,ACT,OP0 dec
    class IMP3,IMP6 bad
    class STAR2,NOVAL,SORTNOTE,CMDANOTE,CMDACOST,MEMO,BADGE,SLEEP note
    class GI0,REV,MV0 drill
    class ENTER,DONE term
